# Copy this file to backend/.env and fill in what you need.
# backend/.env is gitignored — never commit a real key.
#
# The operations assistant answers most questions itself by querying the
# database. Questions it cannot parse are passed to a language model, grounded
# on a live snapshot of the backlog. Nothing here is required: with no model
# available the assistant still runs, it just replies "I could not work out
# what you are asking" for anything outside the intents it handles itself.

# --- Ollama (default, free, runs on this machine) --------------------------
# Needs `ollama serve` running and the model pulled (`ollama pull llama3`).
# Both lines are optional; these are the defaults.
# OLLAMA_URL=http://localhost:11434
# OLLAMA_MODEL=llama3

# --- Claude (optional, paid, better answers) -------------------------------
# If this key is set AND the account has credit, Claude is used first and
# Ollama becomes the backup. Requires credits at console.anthropic.com
# (Plans & Billing) — a valid key with a zero balance is rejected.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# --- Deployment ---------------------------------------------------------
# All optional for local dev — the app falls back to localhost defaults for
# every one of these. Set them when running against a deployed stack.

# Hosted libSQL (Turso) connection. Unset → uses the local database/lumen.db
# file, same as before this existed. `turso db create` / `turso db tokens
# create` prints these.
# TURSO_DATABASE_URL=
# TURSO_AUTH_TOKEN=

# Comma-separated origins allowed to send credentialed requests (CORS).
# Set to the deployed frontend URL(s) in production.
# FRONTEND_ORIGIN=http://localhost:5173

# Base URL of the AI service (FastAPI). Set to the Hugging Face Space URL
# in production.
# AI_SERVICE_URL=http://localhost:8100

# Signs session tokens — set a real random value in production; the
# checked-in default is for local dev only.
# LUMEN_SESSION_SECRET=
